course: dictionary
lesson: 11286
title: Meet the wrongdoer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wrongdoer is a person who does something bad or against the law. The word is made of wrong and doer, so a wrongdoer is someone who does wrong.
explain: Read the context: «Restorative justice brings the wrongdoer and the person harmed together to put things right.» The clue is «the person harmed» and «put things right»: the wrongdoer is the one who caused the harm.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Punishment can protect people and help the wrongdoer change.» If you put "person who did something wrong" in place of wrongdoer, the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Stories and everyday talk often say "the bad guy" or "the person who did it" instead. Wrongdoer is a more formal word, so you will meet it most in news, law and older writing.
fact: A wrongdoer is a person who does something bad or against the law.
fact: In older and church language, wrongdoers means sinners: people who do wrong in God's eyes.
fact: «Wrongdoers» is the plural, so it means more than one wrongdoer.
fact: «Wrongdoer» is a slightly formal word; "the bad guy" is the everyday choice.
fact: Two useful phrases are «punish the wrongdoer» and «bring wrongdoers to justice».
exercise: «Restorative justice brings the wrongdoer and the person harmed together to put things right.» Who is the wrongdoer in this sentence? | The person who was harmed | The friend who helped everyone | The judge who writes the rules | *The person who caused the harm
exercise: What does wrongdoer mean? | A person who fixes broken things | A person who is lost on a walk | A person who tells the time | *A person who does something bad or against the law
exercise: In a story, what everyday words could you use instead of wrongdoer? | the hero | the lunch box | *the bad guy | the weather
test: «If someone is in danger or being hurt, you should go straight to a trusted adult rather than talking to the wrongdoer first.» What is the best thing to do? | Keep it secret from everyone | Talk to the wrongdoer first | *Go straight to a trusted adult | Wait and see what happens
test: In older church language, what are wrongdoers called? | Farmers | Kings | *Sinners | Saints
exam: What does it mean to bring wrongdoers to justice? | To let wrongdoers go home early | To give wrongdoers a big party | *To make people who did wrong face fair consequences through the law | To hide wrongdoers from the police
